                            <comment id="492696" author="ssmirnov" created="Wed, 8 Apr 2026 17:57:38 +0000">&lt;p&gt;Steps to reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Bring up LNet, have at least one local NI configured&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Verify that the local NI status is "up"&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use "ip link set" to bring the link associated with the NI to "down". (This should work with both tcp and o2ib lnets).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use " lnetctl net show" to verify that the local NI status is now "down", ("fatal" flag should be set, visible with -v4 option)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use "ip link set" to bring the same link back "up"&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use " lnetctl net show" to check the NI status. &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
